Syntax: psidrain <victim>

Psionic drain allows the psionicist to siphon mental energy directly
from a target's mind, replenishing their own reserves at the victim's
expense. This vampiric power literally drains the victim's mana while
simultaneously inflicting damage from the mental intrusion.

A successful drain transfers a portion of the victim's mental energy
to the psionicist, restoring their mana. The transfer also deals damage
and temporarily affects the victim's agility as their mind struggles
to compensate for the sudden loss of psychic energy.

Victims cannot be drained repeatedly in quick succession - there is a
recovery period during which the mind resists further draining attempts.
Mindless creatures and dumb animals provide significantly less energy
when drained, as their minds hold less to take.

The power initiates combat if the psionicist is not already engaged
with the target. If used in combat, it can be directed at the current
opponent without specifying a target.

Certain beings, particularly mindflayers, possess a more terrible form
of this power. They can only drain incapacitated victims, but extract
both life force and mental energy through their alien physiology.
Their draining is far more intimate and horrifying to witness.

This power cannot be used while focusing your mind.

